# Section-by-Section Page Improvement Rule

When I provide a page name and section title, only edit that specific section unless I clearly ask for a full-page change.

## Main Goal

Improve each selected section so it feels premium, modern, polished, creative, and visually stronger while keeping the existing site structure and functionality intact.

## Strict Editing Scope

When I give a page name and section title:

1. Locate the exact section.
2. Improve only that section.
3. Keep the rest of the page unchanged.
4. Do not make broad redesign decisions outside the requested section.
5. Briefly explain what was changed.
6. Mention any files edited.

## Visual Quality Rules

For the selected section:

- Improve layout, spacing, alignment, padding, margins, and visual hierarchy.
- Make typography stronger, cleaner, and more premium.
- Improve grammar, wording, headings, CTAs, and supporting text.
- Strengthen font weights, line heights, letter spacing, and heading scale.
- Improve background colours and section contrast.
- Add subtle flair such as dividers, badges, premium cards, animated accents, glow lines, or decorative shapes.
- If a section looks boring, be creative and make it feel more custom, polished, and brand-led.
- Keep animations smooth, subtle, and professional.
- Make the section fully responsive across desktop, laptop, tablet, and mobile.

## Important Contrast Rule

Never place dark text on a dark background.

Always check contrast carefully:

- Dark backgrounds must use white, cream, pale gold, or light text.
- Light backgrounds may use forest green, charcoal, or near-black text.
- Buttons must always have strong readable contrast.
- Green buttons should usually use white or cream text.
- Mustard/gold buttons should use dark green or near-black text.
- Avoid low-contrast muted text that is hard to read.

