## Form Styling Rule

Any form on an edited page should mirror the homepage form style.

Forms should feel consistent across the site:

- Same premium card style.
- Same input styling.
- Same button styling.
- Same spacing and label treatment.
- Same border radius and brand colours.
- Same mobile stacking behavior.
- Same focus states and accessibility.
- Do not create a totally different form design unless I request it.

## Background Rules

Do not use background designs with lines, stripes, wireframes, grids, or busy patterns.

Background sections should use solid colours only.

Preferred section backgrounds:

- Solid deep forest green.
- Solid cream / off-white.
- Solid white.
- Solid charcoal / near-black.
- Solid muted gold only where tasteful.
- Very subtle gradient accents are allowed only for small UI elements, not full busy backgrounds.

Avoid:

- Line-pattern backgrounds.
- Grid backgrounds.
- Cheap neon gradients.
- Overly busy decorative backgrounds.
- Glassmorphism unless I specifically ask.

## Colour Direction

Use the current brand as the base, but improve it with:

- Deep forest green.
- Cream / off-white.
- Mustard / muted gold.
- White.
- Charcoal / near-black.
- Chrome silver accents.
- Blue-to-green gradients.
- Blue-to-silver chrome gradients.
- Green-to-silver chrome gradients.

For existing gradient elements, prefer premium blue / green / silver chrome-style gradients.

Avoid harsh colours or random colours that do not match the brand.

## Section Dividers

Where suitable, add premium section dividers such as:

- Soft curved dividers.
- Thin chrome gradient divider lines.
- Angled background breaks.
- Subtle wave shapes.
- Decorative top/bottom borders.
- Small branded accent strips.

Dividers should improve flow between sections without clutter.

## Typography Rules

Improve copy and typography while keeping the message clear.

- Headings should feel bold, premium, and confident.
- Body text should be easy to read.
- Avoid weak generic wording.
- Fix grammar, spelling, capitalization, and punctuation.
- Improve CTAs so they feel direct and persuasive.
- Use strong but professional language.

## Styling Rules

Do not rebuild the entire app.

Do not change unrelated pages or sections.

Do not remove existing functionality.

Do not change routing, forms, database logic, Supabase logic, Resend logic, auth, or business logic unless I specifically ask.

Do not reduce accessibility.

Do not make the design look like glassmorphism unless I specifically request it.

Avoid overusing shadows, blur, or gradients.

## Responsiveness

Every edited section must look excellent on:

- Large desktop.
- Laptop.
- Tablet.
- Mobile.

Pay special attention to:

- Mobile spacing.
- Heading size.
- Button stacking.
- Image cropping.
- Text contrast.
- Form layout.
- Overflow.
- Tap target sizes.

## Design Feel

The final result should feel like a premium travel, golf, and luxury transfer brand with stronger UI, better spacing, better fonts, richer colours, cleaner cards, subtle motion, polished section transitions, and a more creative high-end feel.